# Label

Renders an accessible caption for a form control. Link it to a control with `for`, or wrap the control inside it. Styled with theme tokens like the shadcn label.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Label } from "#lib/components/ui/label/index.js";
	import { Input } from "#lib/components/ui/input/index.js";
</script>

<Label for="email">Email</Label>
<Input id="email" type="email" placeholder="m@example.com" />
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/label.json
```

## Sizes

Set `size` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`. The default is `md`. Every size uses `--text-sm` except `xs`, which uses `--text-xs`, so the label can match a control of the same size.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Label size="xs" for="name">Name</Label>
<Input size="xs" id="name" />
```

## Icons

Place an icon before or after the text. Icons scale with the label text.

<Demo section="icons" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Label } from "#lib/components/ui/label/index.js";
	import { MailIcon } from "@lucide/svelte";
</script>

<Label for="email"><MailIcon />Email</Label>
```

## Disabled

The label dims and shows a not-allowed cursor when it wraps a disabled control, comes after a disabled sibling control, or sits inside an element with `data-disabled="true"`.

<Demo section="disabled" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Input id="email" disabled />
<Label for="email">Email</Label>

<Label><input type="checkbox" disabled />Remember me</Label>
```

## API

The `Label` props extend the native `label` attributes, such as `for`.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompPropsWithChild<"label"> {
	/** Text size on the shared scale */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Classes merged onto the label */
	class?: CompPropsWithChild<"label">["class"];
}
```
